# Python reference environment (M3) -- regenerate with:
#   & "C:\Users\vegar\.conda\envs\iron\python.exe" -m venv --system-site-packages .venv-ref
.venv-ref/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The build venv. Made and filled by ./bootstrap.sh. `python -m venv` drops a
# self-ignoring .gitignore inside it, so this line is belt-and-braces: the tree
# stays ignored if that file is ever missing (older Python, a copy tool that
# skips dotfiles).
.venv/

# The AMD/Xilinx wheel cache bootstrap.sh downloads into (~1 GB) before it
# verifies their sha256 against requirements.amd.txt. Fully regenerable from
# the pinned URLs, so it is never committed -- the four digests are the
# record, not the bytes.
.wheel-cache/

# Parsed Perfetto traces (~100 MB) are pure derivatives of the raw trace.txt +
# the physical MLIR, both of which ARE committed. Regenerate byte-identically:
#   python experiments\m2-bf16-gemm\regen_trace_json.py
# Verified with --check: all 8 single-core tags match by sha256.
# The whole-array runs (trace_wa*c_*.json) did not copy their physical MLIR, so
# they are NOT regenerable and are committed -- hence the negation below.
experiments/*/artifacts/trace_*.json
!experiments/*/artifacts/trace_wa*.json

# Upstream checkpoints (91 MB for MiniLM). Refetched and re-verified with:
#   & .\.venv-ref\Scripts\python.exe reference\fetch_model.py
# CHECKPOINT.json is committed -- it pins the sha256 the goldens were made
# against, so a swapped checkpoint fails loudly instead of silently.
# (Ignore the CONTENTS, not the directory -- git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, so `models/` alone would hide CHECKPOINT.json too.)
models/**
!models/
!models/*/
!models/*/CHECKPOINT.json
# A whisper model needs SIX small files besides the weights -- config.json
# (geometry), preprocessor_config.json (the audio constants), generation_config.json
# (the decoding policy: suppress_tokens / begin_suppress_tokens), and the
# byte-level BPE table as vocab.json + merges.txt + added_tokens.json. They are
# the same for everyone and 1.5 MB against a 3 GB checkpoint, and committing them
# is what lets a user download model.satetensors, drop it into models/<name>/ and
# run. tokenizer.json, tokenizer_config.json and special_tokens_map.json are NOT
# committed: nothing in the packing path opens them (see kFilesWhisper in
# runtime/src/common/hub.cpp), and tokenizer.json alone is 2.5 MB per model.
# Scoped to the whisper directories on purpose: an embedder's geometry is
# already pinned by its CHECKPOINT.json and is re-read from the checkpoint at
# pack time, so committing its config.json too would be a second copy of a
# number that has one owner.
!models/whisper-*/config.json
!models/whisper-*/generation_config.json
!models/whisper-*/preprocessor_config.json
!models/whisper-*/vocab.json
!models/whisper-*/merges.txt
!models/whisper-*/added_tokens.json

# arch=5 commits preprocessor_config.json for the SAME reason whisper does and
# NOT for the reason config.json would: the image_size, the resample code and
# the mean/std ARE the front end, vit_int8.read_preprocessor() refuses a
# checkpoint that lacks them, and no other file in the tree carries them -- a
# wrong mean yields a container that classifies smoothly and wrongly. 160 bytes.
# config.json stays OUT, exactly as for an embedder above: the geometry has one
# owner (the checkpoint, re-read at pack time) and CHECKPOINT.json pins it.
!models/vit-base-patch16-224/preprocessor_config.json

# Full intermediate tap dump (~54 MB): a deterministic, CPU-only derivative of
# the pinned checkpoint. The committed *_boundary.npz is the contract.
#   & .\.venv-ref\Scripts\python.exe reference\make_goldens.py --taps
reference/goldens/*_taps.npz

# Same idea, EmbeddingGemma-300M spike (tasks/0055) -- ~382 MB, regenerate:
#   & .\.venv-ref\Scripts\python.exe reference\make_goldens_gemma.py --taps
reference/goldens_gemma/*_taps.npz

# Same idea, nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (tasks/0069) -- regenerate:
#   & .\.venv-ref\Scripts\python.exe reference\make_goldens_nomic.py --taps
reference/goldens_nomic/*_taps.npz

# Same policy for arch=3; regenerate:
#   .venv-ref python reference/make_goldens_gte.py --taps
reference/goldens_gte/*_taps.npz

# Exported ONNX graphs -- 90-133 MB each, and a deterministic derivative of a
# sha256-pinned checkpoint, exactly like the taps goldens above.
# bench_cpu_ort.py regenerates them on demand and caches them here.
experiments/m8-npu-vs-cpu/artifacts/onnx/

# Packed runtime weights (68.8 MB): a deterministic derivative of the pinned
# checkpoint. Repack and re-verify with:
#   & "C:\Users\vegar\.conda\envs\iron\python.exe" tools\pack_npue.py
#   & "C:\Users\vegar\.conda\envs\iron\python.exe" tools\verify_npue.py
*.npue

