*.mod*
*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
modules.order
Module.symvers
Mkfile.old
dkms.conf

.idea/
OthersResarch/

# C++ runtime build output and exported designs. The xclbins and instruction
# streams are build artifacts regenerated by:
#   python tools\export_xclbin.py
#   python tools\export_validation.py
runtime/build/
# CMake build directory configured at the repo root (Linux / GCC + XRT in
# /opt/xilinx/xrt). Regenerate with: cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
/build/
# Knowledge-graph output of the `graphify` code-indexing tool (agent aid, not
# part of the build). Regenerated by the tool itself.
/graphify-out/
# Standalone build dir for the EmbeddingGemma tokenizer test CLI
# (tasks/0061), compiled by hand with cl.exe -- not part of the CMake
# npuembeddings target, has no XRT dependency, regenerate per that task's TASK.md.
runtime/build_gemma_tok/
# Standalone build dir for the EmbeddingGemma kernel test CLI (tasks/0063),
# same reasoning as build_gemma_tok/ above -- also holds the generated
# test-vector binary (tools/dump_gemma_kernel_vectors.py), itself derived
# from the sha256-pinned checkpoint, so it stays out of git the same way
# models/** does.
runtime/build_gemma_kernels/
# Standalone build dir for the EmbeddingGemma CPU-encode test CLI
# (tasks/0064), same reasoning as build_gemma_tok/ and build_gemma_kernels/
# above -- also holds ad hoc test corpora and output vectors used only for
# fast local iteration; the ones that matter are copied into the task folder.
runtime/build_gemma_encode/
# EVERY exported design set, however it is suffixed: the plain one, the width
# sweep of tasks/0024 (artifacts1/2/8), the batch sweep of tasks/0025
# (artifacts_b16*) and the minimal-design control (artifacts_pass). A narrower
# pattern, artifacts[0-9]*/, already let artifacts_b16* through once.
#   python tools\export_xclbin.py --cols N --elt-cols M --batch B --out runtime\artifactsX
#   python experiments\m7-switch-cost\build_passthrough.py
runtime/artifacts*/
# ...and the same in the PER-MODEL layout, which is what the exporters write
# now: `runtime/<model>/artifacts_npu<N>/{gemm_rtp,gelu,layernorm,softmax}`.
# The pattern above is anchored at runtime/, so it cannot see one level down --
# which is why a per-model design set was committable.
#   python tools\export_gemm_rtp.py --npu-eltwise --out runtime\<model>
#   python tools\export_eltwise.py --arch all --out runtime\<model>
runtime/*/artifacts*/

# ...and the one design-set layout that is NOT under artifacts*: an int8 ViT
# container needs its OWN set, exported with --int8, because b_layout_hash
# covers the operand dtype (I8 -> 8f858f40..., BF16 -> 52a4adad...) and one set
# serves exactly one of the two. It lands at runtime/<model>-i8/gemm_rtp/ rather
# than under artifacts_npu<N>/ because runtime's fallback scan looks for
# runtime/*/gemm_rtp/design.json two levels down, while the exporter appends
# <model>/artifacts_npu<arch> to whatever --out says, three levels. The layout is
# therefore load-bearing for DISCOVERY, and still a build artifact: 120 KB of
# xclbin and insts bytes bound to this toolchain, regenerated by re-running the
# export. Ignored for the same reason as the bf16 set above.
runtime/*/gemm_rtp/

# Session handoff file. STATE.md says so in its own second line -- "not part of
# the repository: do not commit" -- it is written for the next agent to read and
# rewritten every session, so committing it would put a stale snapshot of
# someone's thinking into the history. Local state, not code.
/STATE.md

# Release staging (tools/make_release.ps1)
dist/

# The public subset, assembled by tools/sync_public_repo.py. It is a BUILD
# OUTPUT of this repository and has its own git history; committing it here
# would duplicate every file.
repo/

# External repos cloned for reference reading only (tasks/0044). Not ours,
# not vendored, not redistributed -- read for architecture and ideas, exactly
# like ../FastFlowLM. Re-clone with tools noted in tasks/0044/TASK.md.
externalrepos/

# Parsed trace for tasks/0130 -- same policy as the experiments traces
# above: a derivative of the committed trace.txt + the committed physical
# MLIR (experiments/m5-pretiled-gemm/artifacts/mlir_pretiled_kn_st_4c_*).
# Regenerate with cfg.trace_to_json(mlir, out) or re-run the traced dispatch.
tasks/0130-t45-traced-roof/trace.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Linux in-source CMake build at runtime/.
#
# The .gitignore already covers the two OUT-of-source layouts -- /build/ at the
# root and runtime/build/ -- because those are what the documented commands use.
# An in-source `cmake -S runtime -B runtime` (or a stray `cd runtime && cmake
# .`) drops the same generated tree next to the sources, and nothing caught it.
# Named file by file rather than globbed: runtime/ also holds hand-maintained
# content, and `runtime/Testing/`-style patterns have a habit of swallowing more
# than they mean to.
#   cmake -S runtime -B runtime -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build runtime
runtime/CMakeCache.txt
runtime/CMakeFiles/
runtime/cmake_install.cmake
runtime/Makefile
# The executable an in-source build leaves in runtime/; an out-of-source one
# puts it under runtime/build/ (already ignored above).
runtime/npuembeddings

# Model download cache (src/common/hub.cpp writes <name>/<file>.part while a
# fetch is in flight and renames on completion). The CHECKPOINTS themselves are
# committed under the top-level models/ -- this is runtime/models/, a different
# path, anchored so the vendored tree above can never be caught by it.
runtime/models/

# Scratch output of ad-hoc harness scripts that write into the CWD they were
# launched from -- runtime/bisect.py posts to a local server and saves the
# responses as res<N>.json here. Real fix is the script writing into a
# temporary directory; ignored until then so a test loop cannot commit noise.
runtime/res*.json

# Agent/tooling config, local to this checkout. AGENTS.md carries the
# code-index instructions the agent runs on, and opencode.jsonc is opencode's
# own project config; neither is project documentation and neither belongs in
# the shared history.
AGENTS.md
opencode.jsonc
